    "segments": [
      {
        "role": "mia",
        "speaker": "Mia",
        "sourceStart": 5,
        "sourceEnd": 54,
        "text": "Hi, Ben. You look tired. Were you waiting for me?",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-JennyNeural",
        "textHash": "fd547b121766858839e9117e50fa23f566e6fb9455ed3fc20ee47a2082ef4be0",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0
      },
      {
        "role": "ben",
        "speaker": "Ben",
        "sourceStart": 60,
        "sourceEnd": 165,
        "text": "Yes, I was. I was standing near the gate for twenty minutes. While I was waiting, I watched the lanterns.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-EricNeural",
        "textHash": "e49e077a812c06ac61321a43dbdf78f9dbce616fe2908c070d66e42c8ef7a4ae",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "mia",
        "speaker": "Mia",
        "sourceStart": 171,
        "sourceEnd": 303,
        "text": "Sorry! My grandmother was telling me a story about this festival. She says the lanterns are for a clever girl who saved our village.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-JennyNeural",
        "textHash": "c1fa9d8425a48e737461e167fbd65b650b30d4e8ea65fd246979a449159c08c2",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "ben",
        "speaker": "Ben",
        "sourceStart": 309,
        "sourceEnd": 429,
        "text": "That's interesting. My neighbor told me a different story. He says the lanterns are for a brave man who fought a dragon.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-EricNeural",
        "textHash": "08927e65599babe801ffa664650f67709db9e34c77b466e624ed2627caf208f4",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "mia",
        "speaker": "Mia",
        "sourceStart": 435,
        "sourceEnd": 463,
        "text": "Really? Which story is true?",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-JennyNeural",
        "textHash": "5604d0a4ade978e3dcd2c6a9f90310a8d382a60ecdb25589810e63f3902c3341",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "ben",
        "speaker": "Ben",
        "sourceStart": 469,
        "sourceEnd": 566,
        "text": "I don't know. Maybe both stories are old. People tell different stories about the same tradition.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-EricNeural",
        "textHash": "f93a3875099312de492a43157f795cd26bc3164534c0315c38ce0e1eda75e8dd",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "mia",
        "speaker": "Mia",
        "sourceStart": 572,
        "sourceEnd": 696,
        "text": "My grandmother's story is about a girl who made a big fire on the hill. The fire helped travelers who were lost in the dark.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-JennyNeural",
        "textHash": "17f285fe4da21fdf1bdcfe12ce56cc2d0bf2460b7a2e772f6a9a43a85e03f752",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "ben",
        "speaker": "Ben",
        "sourceStart": 702,
        "sourceEnd": 839,
        "text": "My neighbor's story is about a man who carried a lantern to the top of the hill. He wanted to warn people about a dragon that was coming.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-EricNeural",
        "textHash": "a39a13dcb97a13cf6754511b24566757d1359854f04166bc98d9c9c93aee2bca",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "mia",
        "speaker": "Mia",
        "sourceStart": 845,
        "sourceEnd": 955,
        "text": "Hmm. Both stories have a hill and a light. Maybe they are the same story, but people remember different parts.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-JennyNeural",
        "textHash": "3af2f62547cb1008d0ac5e15425fed1cd8673589693a8adf5abcccab3aba7232",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "ben",
        "speaker": "Ben",
        "sourceStart": 961,
        "sourceEnd": 1063,
        "text": "That's possible. While we were talking, the sun went down. Look, people are lighting the lanterns now.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-EricNeural",
        "textHash": "8b61c9aa2d4f286bf516eabcc9c95b9bf8ef1bfe2421f8ac574c850ba8a759b7",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "mia",
        "speaker": "Mia",
        "sourceStart": 1069,
        "sourceEnd": 1124,
        "text": "The lanterns are beautiful. Which one do you like best?",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-JennyNeural",
        "textHash": "82148fea26cc4c3bbafcd6a68d40157724ede15bed83f0ffc8b82c2129219ee2",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "ben",
        "speaker": "Ben",
        "sourceStart": 1130,
        "sourceEnd": 1192,
        "text": "I like the red one that is shaped like a fish. What about you?",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-EricNeural",
        "textHash": "56ab7840e7278ba0a18310947028646952dcc260322385f87d1886e9f71f1387",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "mia",
        "speaker": "Mia",
        "sourceStart": 1198,
        "sourceEnd": 1278,
        "text": "I like the small white one which is hanging near the tree. It looks like a star.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-JennyNeural",
        "textHash": "6336902a8ac1a4b52a5234a2dc5d2a9af759511cd2129b81487640a89a82c5a7",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "ben",
        "speaker": "Ben",
        "sourceStart": 1284,
        "sourceEnd": 1316,
        "text": "Do you think the stories matter?",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-EricNeural",
        "textHash": "c5cc5a42d79afe8cd997fa9782f0cb9cae2c9c47f6fcfdecc0037e95e4dba5df",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "mia",
        "speaker": "Mia",
        "sourceStart": 1322,
        "sourceEnd": 1407,
        "text": "Yes. The stories are the reason we come here every year. They connect us to the past.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-JennyNeural",
        "textHash": "0030603d8fa94e33f94db24047a8443692e7fca2352efadab4bf0aa68b6b29db",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "ben",
        "speaker": "Ben",
        "sourceStart": 1413,
        "sourceEnd": 1522,
        "text": "You're right. Next year, I will ask my neighbor more questions. Maybe he knows more about the girl story too.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-EricNeural",
        "textHash": "2e8de5640ee01664cafabcd1a9cf203cbc271d4680d4215025f4a577220196fd",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "mia",
        "speaker": "Mia",
        "sourceStart": 1528,
        "sourceEnd": 1631,
        "text": "Good idea. And I will ask my grandmother about the dragon story. Maybe the two stories will become one.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-JennyNeural",
        "textHash": "73a1ce76d3501feb3013a05be0d638b4fba7bfbf08ba611ceb28a7a979c2b6f8",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      }
    ]
  },
